1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:02,235
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:02,299 --> 00:00:04,359
Pip pushes his fridge door gently.

3
00:00:04,619 --> 00:00:07,309
It swings shut by itself, and stays closed.

4
00:00:07,579 --> 00:00:09,479
There is no lock and no catch.

5
00:00:09,749 --> 00:00:11,179
What keeps it closed?

6
00:00:11,225 --> 00:00:13,065
One, the cold air inside.

7
00:00:14,135 --> 00:00:15,865
Two, a strip of magnet.

8
00:00:16,915 --> 00:00:18,345
Three, sticky glue.

9
00:00:19,593 --> 00:00:21,103
Hold on to your answer!

10
00:00:23,325 --> 00:00:25,125
Today is our magnet hunt!

11
00:00:25,315 --> 00:00:27,585
Where are the magnets hiding in my home?

12
00:00:28,007 --> 00:00:30,457
A little honeybee is hiding in this video.

13
00:00:30,717 --> 00:00:31,947
Can you spot it?

14
00:00:32,297 --> 00:00:33,767
Bees love flowers.

15
00:00:33,837 --> 00:00:35,257
Check near the window!

16
00:00:35,538 --> 00:00:36,998
You against the Buddies!

17
00:00:37,268 --> 00:00:39,118
Lock in first with your fingers.

18
00:00:39,388 --> 00:00:41,218
One finger for every point.

19
00:00:41,874 --> 00:00:43,024
Today you'll learn:

20
00:00:43,226 --> 00:00:44,496
Magnets at home.

21
00:00:44,823 --> 00:00:46,329
Whiteboards and doorstops.

22
00:00:46,734 --> 00:00:48,044
Magnetic or not?

23
00:00:48,544 --> 00:00:49,484
Are you ready?

24
00:00:49,924 --> 00:00:50,694
Three!

25
00:00:51,074 --> 00:00:51,734
Two!

26
00:00:52,104 --> 00:00:52,754
One!

27
00:00:53,174 --> 00:00:53,894
Go!

28
00:00:55,383 --> 00:00:56,273
Round one!

29
00:00:56,583 --> 00:00:58,583
What keeps Pip's fridge door closed?

30
00:00:58,863 --> 00:01:00,693
One, the cold air inside.

31
00:01:00,973 --> 00:01:02,693
Two, a strip of magnet.

32
00:01:02,953 --> 00:01:04,343
Three, sticky glue.

33
00:01:04,643 --> 00:01:05,953
Show me your fingers!

34
00:01:11,473 --> 00:01:12,453
Locked in!

35
00:01:12,731 --> 00:01:13,441
Three!

36
00:01:13,541 --> 00:01:15,521
The door is so hard to pull open.

37
00:01:15,711 --> 00:01:16,921
It must be glue!

38
00:01:17,268 --> 00:01:18,148
Two.

39
00:01:18,318 --> 00:01:21,128
My steel spoon sticks to the door's soft edge.

40
00:01:21,482 --> 00:01:22,252
Two.

41
00:01:22,342 --> 00:01:25,722
Glue would get messy, and cold air cannot hold a door.

42
00:01:26,370 --> 00:01:27,850
Be the magnetic strip!

43
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:29,110
Shrink down.

44
00:01:29,390 --> 00:01:30,320
Quietly.

45
00:01:32,604 --> 00:01:36,574
You are a long, thin magnet, hidden inside the soft edge of

46
00:01:36,594 --> 00:01:37,694
the fridge door.

47
00:01:38,484 --> 00:01:40,394
You go all the way round the door.

48
00:01:41,025 --> 00:01:42,260
The door swings.

49
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:45,020
The fridge's steel body comes closer.

50
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:49,365
You pull towards it, and the edge presses on it, snug.

51
00:01:50,066 --> 00:01:51,676
The door stays closed.

52
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:54,076
The cold air stays in.

53
00:01:55,938 --> 00:01:58,438
The answer is two: a strip of magnet!

54
00:01:58,698 --> 00:02:00,278
Did you show two fingers?

55
00:02:00,518 --> 00:02:01,958
Put one finger up!

56
00:02:02,311 --> 00:02:05,911
A magnetic strip is a long, thin magnet, such as the strip

57
00:02:05,931 --> 00:02:08,641
hidden inside our fridge door's soft edge!

58
00:02:09,370 --> 00:02:10,690
But where is the magnet?

59
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:11,910
I can't see it!

60
00:02:12,790 --> 00:02:13,940
Look closer.

61
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:18,350
Inside the door's soft edge is a long magnetic strip.

62
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:20,930
It goes all the way round the door.

63
00:02:21,255 --> 00:02:23,601
The fridge's body is made of steel.

64
00:02:23,621 --> 00:02:27,729
The strip is attracted to the steel, so the door stays closed,

65
00:02:27,749 --> 00:02:29,774
and the cold air stays in.

66
00:02:32,865 --> 00:02:34,115
Say it with me!

67
00:02:34,825 --> 00:02:38,945
Strips of magnets can be found inside the doors of a refrigerator.

68
00:02:39,685 --> 00:02:41,865
These help to keep the door closed.

69
00:02:44,489 --> 00:02:46,279
Magnets stick to anything shiny!

70
00:02:46,449 --> 00:02:49,349
So my magnet will stick to this shiny window frame!

71
00:02:49,621 --> 00:02:51,181
Something is not right.

72
00:02:51,451 --> 00:02:53,631
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

73
00:02:53,911 --> 00:02:54,871
Hold on!

74
00:03:00,284 --> 00:03:01,414
Arms crossed?

75
00:03:01,684 --> 00:03:02,894
One finger up!

76
00:03:03,171 --> 00:03:05,541
The window frame is made of aluminium.

77
00:03:05,611 --> 00:03:09,841
Aluminium is not a magnetic material, so the magnet is not attracted

78
00:03:09,861 --> 00:03:10,601
to it.

79
00:03:10,874 --> 00:03:12,414
Shiny is not the clue.

80
00:03:12,694 --> 00:03:16,734
Only magnetic materials, like iron and steel, are attracted.

81
00:03:17,248 --> 00:03:19,048
A whiteboard looks like plastic.

82
00:03:19,138 --> 00:03:21,158
So why does Momo's magnet stick?

83
00:03:22,038 --> 00:03:23,188
Look closer.

84
00:03:23,778 --> 00:03:27,208
Under the white writing surface is a thin sheet of steel.

85
00:03:27,778 --> 00:03:30,558
The magnet is attracted to the steel sheet.

86
00:03:30,917 --> 00:03:34,377
Some whiteboards have steel sheets under the writing surfaces.

87
00:03:34,647 --> 00:03:37,777
These allow magnets to be attracted to the whiteboards.

88
00:03:38,366 --> 00:03:41,886
A magnetic whiteboard is a whiteboard with a steel sheet under its

89
00:03:41,906 --> 00:03:45,656
writing surface, such as the board in my study corner!

90
00:03:46,384 --> 00:03:48,114
And look at Pip's bedroom door.

91
00:03:48,724 --> 00:03:52,494
A gust of wind blows in, but the door does not slam.

92
00:03:53,074 --> 00:03:56,634
The magnet on the doorstop holds the door's steel plate.

93
00:03:56,920 --> 00:04:00,590
A magnetic doorstop is a doorstop with a magnet that holds the

94
00:04:00,610 --> 00:04:04,090
door open, such as the one by Pip's bedroom door!

95
00:04:07,387 --> 00:04:08,547
Say it with me!

96
00:04:09,256 --> 00:04:12,456
The magnet on a doorstop helps to hold the door in place

97
00:04:12,476 --> 00:04:14,876
and prevents it from closing suddenly.

98
00:04:17,429 --> 00:04:18,889
Show me your score hand!

99
00:04:19,169 --> 00:04:20,199
Two fingers?

100
00:04:20,479 --> 00:04:21,849
You beat the Buddies.

101
00:04:22,129 --> 00:04:23,129
High five!

102
00:04:23,782 --> 00:04:25,252
Did you spot the honeybee?

103
00:04:25,532 --> 00:04:27,342
It was on the edge of the curtain!

104
00:04:27,620 --> 00:04:29,100
Here is a fun fact!

105
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:33,380
Scientists think honeybees can feel the Earth's magnetism, a little like a

106
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:35,090
compass inside them!

107
00:04:35,291 --> 00:04:36,571
Tell someone at home!

108
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:39,500
Let's read today's key words together!

109
00:04:39,790 --> 00:04:40,550
Ready?

110
00:04:40,837 --> 00:04:42,137
Magnetic strip.

111
00:04:43,902 --> 00:04:45,412
Magnetic whiteboard.

112
00:04:47,394 --> 00:04:48,874
Magnetic doorstop.

113
00:04:50,872 --> 00:04:51,812
Well done!

114
00:04:52,609 --> 00:04:53,979
Look at this train!

115
00:04:54,199 --> 00:04:57,149
It floats above its track, with no wheels touching!

116
00:04:57,424 --> 00:04:58,914
How can a train float?

117
00:04:59,184 --> 00:05:00,774
Find out in Part Two!

118
00:05:02,033 --> 00:05:03,134
Say it with us!

119
00:05:03,934 --> 00:05:04,684
Ready?

120
00:05:04,807 --> 00:05:05,467
One!

121
00:05:05,807 --> 00:05:06,507
two!

122
00:05:06,812 --> 00:05:07,987
Now you know!
